<!-- formalization -->

**Theorem (`scottOpen_Ici_of_compact`).** The principal upset of a compact element is Scott-open.

*Proof.* Compactness supplies a member of any directed set meeting the upset that already lies in the upset, and principal upsets are upper sets. ∎

**Theorem (`compact_wayBelow`).** A compact element lying below \(y\) is way-below \(y\).

*Proof.* The principal upset of the compact element is Scott-open, contains \(y\), and is contained in the principal upset of the compact element. ∎

**Theorem (`isContinuousLattice_of_algebraic`).** Every algebraic complete lattice is a continuous lattice.

*Proof.* Compact elements below \(y\) are way-below \(y\), and algebraicity expresses \(y\) as their directed supremum. ∎

**Definition (`idealCompletion_to_continuousLattice`).** The continuous-lattice structure on an algebraic complete lattice is the one obtained from the preceding theorem.
